So. Renee the Ranger ascended.

This was a straightforward game, nothing exciting except for the 
plethora of artifact weapons that kept showing up. Magicbane, Cleaver, 
and Dragonbane came from early sacrifices on an altar on DL1. MB was my 
early weapon. A bones file around DL12 gave me FireBrand, cursed (and 
also a cursed magic marker). A brief visit to the first level of the 
Quest at XL 12 gave me Ogresmasher from a centaur. Then Sting was 
sitting on the floor (cursed, -1) around Dl14. A bunch of sacrifices on 
DL 18 gave me Frostbrand, and I retired MB as my main weapon. Later, a 
carnivorous ape on the first level of Vlad's tower added Giantslayer to 
the game. 

What the RNG gave in weapons, it made up in other magical items and 
features. This dungeon had no Ludios, no throne rooms, no optional bee 
hives or *trice dens, no optional barracks, no leprechaun halls, no 
sinks, nothing-- just one level of swamps. This dungeon also had very 
little magical armor (the speed boots I ascended with were the only 
magical footwear other than elven boots that I saw until after the 
Castle; I never saw a HoB or HoTele and din't find HoOA until deep in 
Gehennom; GoP and GoD also didn't show up until well into Gehennom; I 
never saw an oilskin cloak --or an oilskin sack, for that matter, and 
the only (BoH was the one I wished up; never saw an "AoMB.) and what 
seemed like not a lot of scrolls or potions. 

I had fun at the Castle playing Mastermind with a bugle and drawbridging 
various Ls and Hs (genocided the Ls later, though). Castle wand was at 
0:1, and wishes went for 2 bl?Charging and a blessed greased (BoH. (A 
brief detour to remap dungeon levels after a MF encounter later gave me 
another /WoW (0:1) from a gnome king on the Oracle level.) The castle 
had both silver and grey dragons, so I got GDSM to go along with my [SoR 
and "AoR.

VoD showed me that my [CoDisplacement wasn't really up to Gehennom; I 
kept losing and regaining XL 15 from the wraith attacks, Meanwhile. by 
this time I'd found +magic mapping and +detect treasure, but with Int 15 
and XL 15 couldn't cast them at all (100% fail). I #enchanted divination 
spells to basic and still couldn't manage what I wanted (still 100% fail 
for mapping), and of course there were no robes in the dungeon, so I 
tamed a dog, hauled it back up to Minetown (no magic whistle, no 
surprise), tried to get the dog to attack the minetown priest, hauled it 
back out of Minetown to the first level of the Quest which was the only 
poly trap I could remember, got the large dog (XL9, 72 HP or so) turned 
into a leocrotta (XL8, ~61 HP, but more attacks per round than a dog), 
hauled it back to Minetown, and discovered that it still wouldn't attack 
the Minetown priest. One =conflict later, I had a live leocrotta and a 
dead priest and a robe, and I still couldn't cast mapping reliably 
(IIRC, still at least 90% fail, may actually have been 100%). I cast 
lots of +light for the experience, #enhanced divination spells to 
Skilled, and finally had +mapping at 0% fail. Okay.

Gehennom was shorter than usual from the bottom up, Vlad was no problem, 
I paid off Baalzebub and Asmodeus, lalala. Rodney went down to a /Death 
at turn 79023, then again at the VS at turn 79208 and with two zaps in 
Moloch's at turn 79216. At this point I was getting worried that my two 
/Death and two ?charging wouldn't be enough. But the force wasn't 
terrible and I saw Rodney again only in the VoD and on Fire. Air took 
two !FH (at 140/290 and 81/290), and somewhere in there I evidently 
reached XL16 in melee.

On Astral, Death was left, Famine, center, and Pestilence right, and I 
entered at the center. Famine's altar was lawful. Second altar I tried 
was Pestilence's (needed another two !FH to get there), and a choir sang 
and all that.

Some day, I'll learn to play faster-- this game was 81392 turns, which 
is long even for me.

Twelve down, Healer to go.

